reagent-name-dh-ketorolac = ketorolac
reagent-desc-dh-ketorolac = A non-steroidal painkiller: weak, but long-lasting and not habit-forming. Hinders clotting, so avoid it when the patient is bleeding.
reagent-name-dh-tramadol = tramadol
reagent-desc-dh-tramadol = A weak opioid with moderate pain relief. Tolerance builds slowly. An overdose causes seizures.
reagent-name-dh-fentanyl = fentanyl
reagent-desc-dh-fentanyl = A very strong opioid that works in small doses. From 8 units in the blood it depresses breathing. The antidote is naloxone.
reagent-name-dh-ketamine = ketamine
reagent-desc-dh-ketamine = Field anaesthesia: strong pain relief, and from 10 units in the blood the patient goes under, ready for surgery.
reagent-name-dh-etamsylate = etamsylate
reagent-desc-dh-etamsylate = A long-acting haemostatic: gradually stops bleeding and slows internal bleeding.
reagent-name-dh-ringer = Ringer's solution
reagent-desc-dh-ringer = A salt solution that restores blood volume, a little better than saline.
reagent-name-dh-colloid = colloid solution
reagent-desc-dh-colloid = Hydroxyethyl starch: stays in the vessels and quickly restores blood volume. Over 40 units hinders clotting.
reagent-name-dh-albumin = albumin
reagent-desc-dh-albumin = A blood protein that restores volume and brings the patient out of shock after blood loss.
reagent-name-dh-norepinephrine = norepinephrine
reagent-desc-dh-norepinephrine = Keeps blood pressure up in shock and critical condition. An overdose strains the heart.
reagent-name-dh-atropine = atropine
reagent-desc-dh-atropine = An antidote for poisoning that supports breathing. An overdose causes tremors.
reagent-name-dh-propofol = propofol
reagent-desc-dh-propofol = Intravenous anaesthesia for surgery: the patient sleeps while it is in the blood. Depresses breathing.
reagent-name-dh-midazolam = midazolam
reagent-desc-dh-midazolam = A sedative that calms tremors and agitation. From 15 units it puts the patient to sleep.
reagent-name-dh-naloxone = naloxone
reagent-desc-dh-naloxone = Reverses opioids and the breathing problems they cause. Triggers withdrawal in dependent patients.
reagent-name-dh-flumazenil = flumazenil
reagent-desc-dh-flumazenil = Reverses sedatives: midazolam, propofol and ketamine.
reagent-name-dh-dexamethasone = dexamethasone
reagent-desc-dh-dexamethasone = A steroid against swelling and inflammation: moderately treats burns, chemical burns and allergies.
reagent-name-dh-prussianblue = Prussian blue
reagent-desc-dh-prussianblue = Binds radioactive isotopes and flushes out radiation.
